Task 1: Requirement Analysis and Network Architecture
1.1 Introduction
TechNova Solutions Pvt. Ltd. is an IT company headquartered in Guwahati, Assam, with a branch office in Jorhat. The company has a total of 130 employees, out of which 100 employees work at the Guwahati head office and 30 employees work at the Jorhat branch office.
As the company is expanding its operations, it needs a well-organized, secure, and reliable computer network. At present, employees are facing problems such as slow internet speed, unauthorized access to confidential files, poor connectivity between the two offices, and network interruptions due to device failures.
To solve these problems, I propose a network infrastructure that provides better connectivity, strong security, centralized data management, and easy communication between both offices.
The proposed network will also support future requirements such as video conferencing, cloud-based applications, online collaboration, and remote working.
1.2 Networking Requirements of the Company
After analyzing the given situation, I have identified the following major networking requirements:
1. High-speed internet connectivity
The company needs a high-speed internet connection to ensure that employees can work smoothly without facing slow internet during office hours. A business-grade broadband or leased-line connection can be used.
2. Department-wise network security
The head office has five departments:
•	Human Resources (HR)
•	Finance and Accounts
•	Software Development
•	Marketing and Sales
•	Administration
Each department should have separate network access so that employees cannot access confidential information belonging to other departments without permission.
3. Secure connection between both offices
The Guwahati head office and Jorhat branch office must be connected through a secure WAN connection. A site-to-site VPN can be implemented to allow employees to share company resources safely.
4. Remote access for employees
Employees working from home should be able to access company files and applications securely. For this purpose, a remote-access VPN with multi-factor authentication (MFA) can be provided.
5. Network reliability
The network should continue working even if a particular networking device or internet connection fails. Backup internet connections and redundant networking devices should be used to reduce downtime.
6. Support for modern applications
The network should have sufficient bandwidth to support video conferencing, cloud applications, centralized file storage, and online collaboration tools.
7. Strong cybersecurity
The company needs proper security measures to protect its network from unauthorized access, malware, viruses, phishing attacks, and data theft.
8. Scalability
The network should be designed in such a way that new employees, computers, departments, and networking devices can be added easily in the future.
1.3 Recommended Network Topology for the Head Office
I recommend using a Star Topology for the Guwahati head office.
In star topology, all computers and other network devices are connected to a central switch. Each department will have its own network connection through managed switches.
Reasons for selecting Star Topology:
1.	Easy to manage: All computers are connected through central switches, making network management easier.
2.	Easy troubleshooting: If one computer or cable stops working, the other computers can continue working normally.
3.	Better performance: Managed switches provide efficient communication between connected devices.
4.	Easy expansion: New computers and devices can be connected without disturbing the existing network.
5.	Improved security: VLANs can be configured to separate different departments and control network access.
6.	Centralized monitoring: The network administrator can monitor connected devices from a central location.
Conclusion: Star topology is suitable for TechNova Solutions because it is simple, reliable, cost-effective, and easy to expand as the company grows.
1.4 Types of Networks Required
The company will require the following types of networks:
1. LAN (Local Area Network)
LAN will be used within each office to connect desktop computers, printers, servers, and other devices. The Guwahati and Jorhat offices will each have their own LAN.
2. WAN (Wide Area Network)
WAN will connect the Guwahati head office with the Jorhat branch office. A site-to-site VPN over business internet connections will provide secure communication between both locations.
3. WLAN (Wireless Local Area Network)
WLAN will provide wireless connectivity to employees using laptops, smartphones, and other wireless devices. Wireless access points will be installed in both offices.
4. VPN (Virtual Private Network)
VPN will provide encrypted communication between the two offices and allow authorized employees to access company resources securely while working from home.
1.5 Roles of Networking Devices and Technologies
The following networking devices and technologies will be used to build the proposed network infrastructure.
1. Router
A router connects different networks and forwards data packets between them. In this company, routers will connect the internal office networks to the internet and establish communication between the Guwahati and Jorhat offices.
2. Switch
A switch connects multiple computers, printers, servers, and other devices within a LAN. Managed switches will be used to connect employees' computers and separate departments using VLANs.
3. Wireless Access Point (WAP)
A wireless access point allows employees to connect laptops, smartphones, and tablets to the company network through Wi-Fi. It will provide wireless connectivity in both offices.
4. Server
Servers will be used to store and manage company data and provide different services to employees. The company can use the following servers:
•	File Server: Stores important company documents and allows authorized employees to access files.
•	Database Server: Stores and manages company information.
•	Application Server: Runs business applications used by employees.
•	Authentication Server: Manages employee login details and access permissions.
•	Backup Server: Maintains copies of important company data to prevent data loss.
5. LAN (Local Area Network)
LAN connects computers and other devices within a limited geographical area, such as an office building. It will help employees communicate and share resources within their respective offices.
6. WAN (Wide Area Network)
WAN connects networks over a large geographical distance. It will connect the Guwahati head office with the Jorhat branch office so that employees can securely share company resources.
7. WLAN (Wireless Local Area Network)
WLAN provides wireless network access to employees. It will allow employees to connect to the company network without using physical network cables.
8. Firewall
A firewall monitors incoming and outgoing network traffic and blocks unauthorized access. It will protect the company's internal network from external threats.
