Explanation of the Network Architecture
The proposed architecture is divided into two main parts: the Guwahati head office and the Jorhat branch office.
A. Head Office – Guwahati
The head office has 100 employees and five departments. It will have the following network arrangements:
1.	A primary and backup internet connection will be connected to the main firewall/router.
2.	The firewall will protect the internal network from unauthorized external access.
3.	A Layer 3 core switch will manage communication between different department networks.
4.	Managed access switches will connect employee computers and other office devices.
5.	Separate VLANs will be created for HR, Finance, Software Development, Marketing and Sales, and Administration.
6.	A centralized server room will contain file, database, authentication, and backup servers.
7.	Wireless access points will provide Wi-Fi connectivity to authorized employees.
B. Branch Office – Jorhat
The Jorhat branch has 30 employees. It will have a separate LAN consisting of employee computers, managed switches, wireless access points, and a firewall/router.
The branch office will connect to the head office using a site-to-site IPsec VPN. This will allow employees to securely access shared files and applications available at the Guwahati head office.
C. Connection Between Both Offices
A secure VPN connection will be established between the two offices using their respective firewall devices.
This connection will encrypt the data transmitted over the internet and help protect confidential company information from unauthorized access.
D. Remote Employees
Employees working from home will connect to the company's network using a remote-access VPN. Multi-factor authentication will be enabled to provide an additional layer of security.
1.7 Department-wise Network Segmentation
To improve security and control unauthorized access, I recommend dividing the head office network into five separate VLANs.
Department	Network Segment
HR	VLAN 10
Finance and Accounts	VLAN 20
Software Development	VLAN 30
Marketing and Sales	VLAN 40
Administration	VLAN 50
Servers	VLAN 60
Guest Wi-Fi	VLAN 70
Each VLAN will have its own network segment. For example, employees working in HR will only be allowed to access HR-related files and applications according to their permissions.
Access between VLANs will be controlled through firewall rules and Layer 3 access control lists (ACLs). Guest Wi-Fi users will be kept separate from the company's internal network.
1.8 Benefits of the Proposed Network Architecture
The proposed network architecture will provide several benefits to TechNova Solutions Pvt. Ltd.
1.	Improved network speed: High-speed internet and managed switches will improve network performance during working hours.
2.	Better data security: VLANs, firewalls, and access control policies will prevent unauthorized access to confidential information.
3.	Reliable communication: The VPN connection will provide secure communication between Guwahati and Jorhat.
4.	Remote working support: Employees will be able to access company resources securely from home.
5.	Reduced downtime: Backup internet connections and redundant networking devices will help maintain network availability.
6.	Centralized data management: Servers will make it easier to store, manage, and back up company information.
7.	Future expansion: The network can support additional employees, devices, and applications as the company grows.
1.9 Conclusion
After analyzing the networking requirements of TechNova Solutions Pvt. Ltd., I recommend implementing a star-based network architecture using LAN, WAN, WLAN, and VPN technologies.
The proposed design will connect the Guwahati head office and Jorhat branch office through a secure VPN connection. Department-wise VLANs will improve network security, while centralized servers will make data management easier.
I have also recommended firewalls, managed switches, wireless access points, and backup internet connections to improve network performance and reliability.
Overall, this network design will provide a secure, efficient, reliable, and scalable networking environment. It will solve the company's existing networking problems and also support its future IT requirements, such as cloud computing, video conferencing, and online collaboration tools.
